<title>FRANCE: Prodi says Europe without Italy weakened - paper.</title>
<headline>Prodi says Europe without Italy weakened - paper.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian Prime Minister Romano Prodi said in a newspaper interview on Thursday that a Europe without Italy would be weakened.</p>
<p>&quot;I am convinced that the future of Italy is with Europe,&quot; he said in an interview with daily Le Figaro.</p>
<p>&quot;I am also convinced that without Italy Europe would be weakened, continually submitted to trade turbulence and serious political problems,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>&quot;Italy is the leading edge of Mediterranean Europe. Everybody, beginning with France needs a stable and united Italy.&quot;</p>
</text>
